From bea6837be0d7bb43d82cbda8ae2decac108816a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Langley <davidl@element.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:40:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Log to the browser console on wasm

The FFI never installed a tracing subscriber on wasm, so nothing the
SDK logged was visible in the browser. `init_platform` now builds the
same subscriber as on other platforms, with the stdout layer writing
each event to the matching `console.*` method, no timestamps (the
console has its own, and `SystemTime::now` isn't available on wasm),
and without `log_panics` or `RUST_BACKTRACE`, which have no
environment to live in there.
